-- title:
--   k(X₁(M)) is finite separable over k(jmath̄)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ (in `Type`). Write $K_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC k M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field `LaurentSeries k` over $k$ obtained by adjoining to $k$ the set [`ModularCurve.intFormRatiosC k (Gamma1 M)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L83) of Laurent series attached to $\Gamma_1(M)$, and let $\bar\jmath =$ [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) be the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image in $k$ of the integral power series [`ModularCurve.jNum`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L142) $= E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$, i.e. the reduction of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. The assertion is that there exists an element $t$ of $K_0$ whose image in `LaurentSeries k` equals $\bar\jmath$, such that $t$ is transcendental over $k$, and such that $K_0$ is a finite-dimensional and separable extension of the simple subextension $k\langle t\rangle = k\,⟮t⟯$ generated by $t$.
--
--   This is the function-field statement underlying the reduction of the modular curve $X_1(M)$ modulo $p \nmid M$: the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$ contains the reduced $j$-invariant, which is a separating transcendental element, and the extension over $k(\bar\jmath)$ is finite and separable. It is the basic input for the construction and analysis of models of $X_1(M)$ and of Hecke correspondences on them in characteristic $p$, and is invoked throughout the subsequent work on $X_1(p)$, its two-chart integral models and the associated Picard groups and inertia computations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_coe_eq_jqModC_and_transcendental_and_finiteDimensional_and_isSeparable_x1FunctionFieldC.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JqCoeff

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
